# Get columns from the AirData .csv and create a new one from selected columns.
# There is a fixed format from Airdata. It may have been augmented with
# columns from the Phantom Help .csv. The table below tells which of those
# augmented columns to also import.
#
# Put augmented column before ('b'), or after ('a') existing column. An
# augmented column can also be deleted ('d').
#
# Target line (0-based), command ('b','e','d'), string if command not 'd'
# The string is the title for the column. A comment can be added after
# the end of the string by appending a '#'. The '#' and everything
# following is ignored.

6,e,trvl hdg/51 # add after compass heading and gimbal heading
15,e,total dst/52 # add after max distance

